{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>How could one chase.</b> The meaning: were Israel wise, they would understand how one of the enemies could chase a thousand of Israel — is it not only because their Rock forsook them? And some say: how was it that at first one of Israel would chase a thousand, and now they grew weak?" "<b>For their Rock sold them.</b> Like \"gave them,\" and likewise \"and YHWH will sell Sisera\" (Judges 4:7). The meaning: as though He gave them as hire for their deeds, and behold, it is an actual sale." "<b>Surrendered them.</b> Like the sense of \"he closes in on a man,\" or like \"and he surrendered to us.\""], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:07.756176747Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}